  "description": "For a hydraulic-press digital twin aimed at predictive maintenance you combine a physics-based, reduced-order press model with a data-driven degradation estimator, both fed by pressure, stroke and temperature telemetry. The physics model gives you a stress field and fatigue index; the data model tracks drift the physics can't see. Fuse the two into a single risk score, gate maintenance alerts on it, and keep every reading in a time-series store for retraining.\n\nBudget roughly USD 15-40k for the first integration plus tool seats; expect 8-12 weeks to a working twin against historian data.",
